<handout component="cur">
    <title>Wednesday 10/14</title>
    <objectives>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <p>
                    Practice problems using implicit differentiation.
                </p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <p>
                    Take second derivatives using implicit differentiation.
                </p>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </objectives>
    <page>
        <paragraphs>
            <title>Implicit Differentiation</title>

<p component="b" workspace="3in">
    Last class, we began our discussion of implicit differentiation. What was this process?
</p>
<p component="a">
    Last class, we began our discussion of implicit differentiation. What was this process? Finding the slope without needing to solve for y first.
</p>

<p component="b" workspace="3in">
    What is the key computational trick in this process?
</p>
<p component="a">
    What is the key computational trick in this process? Differentiate the entire equation. Any term with a <m>y</m> in it requires the Chain Rule.
</p>

        </paragraphs>
    </page>

