    </page>
</handout>

<handout component="cur">
    <title>Friday 10/16</title>
    <objectives>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <p>
                    Apply implicit differentiation to tangent line problems.
                </p>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </objectives>
    <page>
        <example workspace="0in">
            <introduction>
                <p>
                    Consider the equation 
                    <md>
                        x^2 + y^4 - 3xy = 16
                    </md>.
                    
                </p>
            </introduction>
            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        Find <m>\frac{dy}{dx}</m>.
                    </p>
                </statement>
        
            </task>
            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        Find <m>\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}</m>.
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>
        
        </example>
        
    </page>
    <page>
        <paragraphs>
            <title>Applications of Implicit Differentiation</title>

<p component="b" workspace="3in">
    As always, the derivative gives us the slope of the tangent line. This means that we can use it to find the equation of the tangent line.
</p>
<p component="a">
    As always, the derivative gives us the slope of the tangent line. This means that we can use it to find the equation of the tangent line. Slope and point again.
</p>

<example workspace="3in">
    <statement>
        <p>
            Find the equation of the tangent line to the graph of 
            <md>
                x^2 + 4y^3 = 5
            </md> at the point <m>(1,1)</m>.
            
        </p>
    </statement>

</example>


        </paragraphs>
    </page>

    <page>
        <example workspace="4in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    Find the equation of the tangent line to the graph of 
                    <md>
                        \cos(x^2y) - 3x = 5y - 2e^{y} 
                    </md> at the point <m>(1,0)</m>.
                    
                </p>
            </statement>
        
        </example>
        
    </page>

    <page>
        <example workspace="4in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    Find all points where the tangent line to 
                    <md>
                        x^2 - y^2 - 2xy = \frac{9}{2}
                    </md> is horizontal and vertical.
                    
                </p>
            </statement>
        
        </example>
        
    </page>

    <page>
        <example workspace="4in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    Find all points on the graph of 
                    <md>
                        x^2 + 2y^2 = 9
                    </md> where the tangent line goes through the point <m>(5,1)</m>.
                    
                </p>
            </statement>
        
        </example>
        
    </page>
</handout>

</section>